##! Please refer to the documentation at
##! https://coreruleset.org/docs/development/regex_assembly/.

##! The command must fill its own line: it follows the line break directly, and
##! nothing but spaces may follow it before the next line break, or it ends the
##! value. Spaces at the very end of the value are not allowed: a `[ \t]*$` tail
##! backtracks over every space, so a long run hits the PCRE match limit and the
##! whole value goes unchecked. SMTP (RFC 5321) has no command tags, so a word before
##! the command is prose ("...\r\nplease help"), not a tag. Tagged commands are IMAP,
##! see 932310.
##!+ i
##!^ \r\n
##!$ (?:[ \t]*[\r\n]|$)

##! - SMTP Commands without or optional params
DATA
QUIT
##! The bound keeps a long word from backtracking into the match limit.
HELP(?: \S{1,64})?

##! - SMTP Commands with params

##! Not covered -  X<atom> Command (client extensions)
